  "conclusions": [
    "SwNodeNum uses GetTextNode and independent text IsNotifiable/IsNotificationEnabled predicates; roots/phantoms use caller reading then dtor short circuit.",
    "SwTextNode publicly exposes zero-argument bool predicates; m_bNotifiable is private,true by constructor default and separate from global document conditions.",
    "The friend TextNodeNotificationSuppressor saves/clears/restores the temporary flag in native autoattribute construction. This selected policy repair does not certify complete constructor suppressor lifetime.",
    "SwDoc.mbDtor is private,false by constructor default; IsInDtor returns it. Destructor sets true before owned content/node destruction,including later DelNodes.",
    "Local Dispose gains the flag before existing list/undo/state teardown. Full native services/style/redline/undo/client/word-count/layout destruction and post-native-destruction object lifetime are not certified.",
    "No registered document IO/recovery changes,upstream calls by project tests,stored source/helper files or full-module/goal promotion.",
    "Fresh GetRoot and inline InvalidateAndNotifyTree inspection confirms parentless roots return null and do not invalidate/notify; attached records dispatch to the root. Root no-op assertions cover this existing contract. Actual missing coverage after corrected teardown was the independent GetPred no-parent branch; native source returns null for roots/orphans for both sibling modes,now directly asserted without changing core tree code."
